WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:16.413
Fleet settings control how often devices check for updates and
report their health. Use this section to balance visibility,
responsiveness and network cost. A shorter interval gives you
fresher information, while a longer interval reduces reporting
activity.

2
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:29.920
Review the estimate before saving. It is a planning aid based on
the selected settings, not a guaranteed invoice. Approving Save
records the configuration; it does not deposit funds into the
network budget.

3
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:45.659
This demonstration shows a budget warning because the available
funds do not cover the estimate. Saving anyway records the
settings only. Review the warning and fund the budget separately
if you want devices to sustain the planned activity.

4
00:00:46.360 --> 00:01:03.981
Devices pick up the saved configuration at their next check, so
the change is not instantaneous across the fleet. Check the
Devices page for fresh reports, and return to Network budget to
monitor funds. You now have the basic workflow from enrollment
through controlled software delivery.

